1017,2025-04-07 00:00:00,2025,Alleged Deepfake Investment Scam in Spain Defrauds 208 Victims of €19 million ($20.9 million),"Spanish police arrested six individuals allegedly behind a €19M ($20.9M) global investment scam powered by AI. The operation used deepfake ads featuring national celebrities to deceive victims, many of whom were selected through targeting algorithms. Scammers posed as financial advisors and fake officials, cycling through romance baiting, investment fraud, and recovery scams. AI-generated content amplified trust and engagement.","Unnamed Criminal Group In Spain, Individuals Arrested In Granada And Alicante","Deepfake Technology Developers, Generative Ai Developers","General Public, General Public Of Spain, Global Victims Targeted By Scams, Individuals Who Lost Money Through Scam Investment Platforms",642188372947D07020C1319D,"Algorithmic Targeting Tools, Fake Investment Platforms, Identity Spoofing And Impersonation Tools, Deepfake Technology",,"The incident date of 04/07/2025 is taken from the date of the arrests. The scams had been ongoing for at least two years, according to reports.",MIT,2,Malicious Actors & Misuse,"Fraud, scams, and targeted manipulation",Human,Intentional,Post-deployment,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,1,Intentional human misuse
